   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of proposals developed based on programme priority areas identified by ISA</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2019">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Develop two joint proposals</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 2 joint proposals in collaboration with International Solar Alliance developed on disseminating solar technologies in developing countries (signatories of ISA) for supporting poor households</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. project activities will strengthen capacities of ISA and mobilise resources through joint programming and facilitating wider UN system engagement with ISA.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Following final grant approval, the multi-country project on ten countries Scaling Solar Applications for Agricultural Use (SSAAU), is being operationalised. 
2. Ideated concept for new engagement on feasibility study in the 8 pacific SIDs. Engaging vetted consultants from the GPN Express roster. 
3. Engaged a consultant to develop ISAs country partnership strategy (CPS) and mechanisms. Identified key roles for ISAs representation in member countries - NFPs for realising CPS.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened capacities at ISA for effective operationalization of its role
Strengthened programming capacity for scaling solar applications in ISA member countries
Established platforms for visibility, partnerships and South-South Cooperation</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">International consultants were engaged to develop the Country Partnership Strategy and Country Partnership Framework. The draft Strategy and Framework have been shared with ISA for finalisation and for next steps to be is piloted and operationalized in about 15 ISA mmeber countries. 
The pile project on Scaling Solar Applications for Agricultural Use has been initiated with implementation and management modalities discussed and finalised with all ten UNDP CO offices. The feasibility study will be launched in the first month of 2023. Further priorities consistent with the ISA programming framework have been identified and developed (i) ESG study for Solar value chain and (ii) Conduct Feasibility Studies in LDCs and SIDS member countries to identify potential solarization 
of public buildings.
Discussions initiated between ISA , UNDP India CO and the Sustainable Energy Hub@UNDP HQ for increasing the visibility of ISA and for South South Partnerships</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
